.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt TALK 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm talk
.Nd talk to another user
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar address
.Op Ar terminal
.Nm
.Fl l
.Op Ar terminal
.Nm
.Fl -loopback
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility establishes a two-way, screen-oriented session with another user.
The
.Ar address
operand has the form
.Sm off
.Ar user Op @ Ar host .
.Sm on
The optional
.Ar terminal
operand selects one of the recipient's terminals.
.Pp
The caller sends an invitation with the
.Dq "Message from" ,
.Dq "connection requested by"
and
.Dq "respond with"
lines.
The recipient accepts or declines.
Once active, both parties can type simultaneously, and their text is shown in separate regions
of the screen.
The invitation and session are carried by the bounded
.Dq RVTALK/1
protocol.
.Pp
The following controls are handled:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ctrl-C
Send
.Dv BYE
and terminate the local session with status 0.
.It Ctrl-D
End the local input and notify the peer.
.It Ctrl-L
Refresh the local split screen.
.It Ctrl-G
Alert the recipient's terminal.
.El
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l
Listen for an invitation instead of sending one.
This is a local extension; POSIX defines no
.Nm
options.
.It Fl -loopback
Run both ends of the protocol in one process and print a readable transcript.
This is a local diagnostic for the bounded protocol, not a peer session.
.El
.Sh CURRENT LIMITATION
This image has no logged-in terminal registry and no peer transport.
The
.Ql ttyd
service records only a session's foreground group, session id and hangup bit;
.Xr consd 8
serves one console and the
.Ql ptyd
service serves one anonymous master/slave pair.
There is no
.Ql who
terminal list to locate the recipient and no
.Nm talkd
to carry the invitation.
Consequently a local
.Nm
call reports that the recipient is not reachable and exits with status 1;
.Fl l
reports that no peer transport exists.
Network
.Ar host
addresses other than
.Ql localhost
are rejected explicitly.
The local loopback diagnostic is the only complete session path until a
terminal registry and peer transport exist.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A declined invitation, unsupported network address, unreachable recipient,
missing peer transport or protocol failure exits with status 1; a usage error
exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr write 1 ,
.Xr consd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the documented POSIX
.Nm
invitation, split-screen, forwarding, EOF and termination model with the
current-limitation noted above.
